   "notes": "CPU-only automatic fallback exists in the unmodified HTTP server: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/denis-pplx/autojev/ee63c1515980491a742f0bd0685c8dc5ca1f00c3/src/autojev/model.py L123: self.device_name = device or (\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"); L154: dtype = torch.bfloat16 if self.device_name.startswith(\"cuda\") else torch.float32; L174: self.to(self.device_name). https://raw.githubusercontent.com/denis-pplx/autojev/ee63c1515980491a742f0bd0685c8dc5ca1f00c3/src/autojev/server.py L122: service.model = await run_in_threadpool(DecisionModel, checkpoint=service.checkpoint). The server does not expose device selection and chooses only cuda/cpu, so no MPS variant is added. CPU loads FP32: ~104.35 GB weights, ~130.43 GB with 25% allowance, so this is a technically supported high-memory route, not practical on ordinary laptops. In-process trained head => backend_agnostic=false. Memory estimate: 52.173 GB downloaded weights × 2 for fp32 × 1.25 working-memory allowance; minimum RAM rounded up with OS/runtime allowance. Image requests, long contexts and concurrent questions can need more. Windows means WSL2 with CPU PyTorch; native Windows dependencies were not verified.",
